nd they cut the pay and they  made it a pretty unglamorous job waiting  for the industry to recover they became  instructors eventually opening their own  flight school in 2016. it's a really  exciting way to share your passion and  then at the same time be able to make a  living at it but once they train their  flight instructors it's tough to keep  them we're hoping to you know get more  applicants in to  you know feel that  the vacuum really  the airlines are they're taking people  really really fast right now the  airlines are in a full-on hiring frenzy  due to the mandatory 65 year old  retirement age most airlines projecting  a pilot shortage over the next decade  more than 800 000 pilots will be needed  with more than two hundred thousand in  the us there are only about sixty five  thousand female pilots in the world  which accounts for nine percent of the  total out of the thirteen thousand  pilots in the u.s only nine hundred of  them are women so i'm hoping being a  woman in aviation as there's not too  many of us that that helps me  move through the ranks faster experts  say with continued efforts in education  and outreach we can expect to see more  women in the cockpit and in other higher  profile aviation roles as well there's  so much to learn danielle is up for the  challenge 1500 flight hours among other  credentials she hopes to complete this  by the time she turns 35 and has this  advice for other women don't give up if  someone tells you you can't you  absolutely can i had i have two kids i  was a single mom for most of my flight  training you can absolutely do it i work  full time i fly there's nothing stopping  you besides you so just push through it  kiersten joyce live local now  now airlines are trying to help bridge  the gap just this year united started  teaching students at its own flight  school in arizona with the goal of  training 5 thousand pilots by 2030. the  company aiming for half of that number  to be women and people of color united  even covers the cost of pilots training  up to the point of receiving their  private pilot's license

